The portable shader retains core 32-bit arithmetic and shared-memory reductions.
The optional split-K shader uses independent 32-thread workgroups, requesting
wave32 only when advertised; ordered reduction is fused into post-Hadamard.
No cooperative-matrix feature is required.
The optional native codebook shader also adapts the paired FP16 addition
algorithm from exl3_common.glsl at the same revision; FP32 accumulation and
the portable LUT fallback remain available.

The LFM3 computation order follows LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, source revision
0dc4268b561499c648c7ba7c9466bf3d8d01517a, modeling_lfm3.py (Apache-2.0,
Copyright 2026 The HuggingFace Team) and ExLlamaV3 1.6.6 architecture/lfm3.py
(MIT). LFM3 model weights retain their own license and are not bundled.
